.TH TS2MKV 1 "2026-10-10" "ts2mkv" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ts2mkv \- losslessly remux MPEG-TS captures to Matroska
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ts2mkv
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR|\fIDIR\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ts2mkv
remuxes MPEG-TS captures
.RI ( .ts / .mts )
into Matroska
.RB ( .mkv )
without re-encoding the video: the compressed bitstream is copied verbatim, so
the operation is fast and incurs no generation loss. For each input it selects
the first video stream and the first audio stream, which discards the
duplicate or multi-program streams common in raw captures and produces a clean
single-program MKV.
.P
Video is always copied. Audio is copied too, but if the source audio has
unparseable ADTS headers (common in TS captures) the Matroska muxer can abort,
so the file is retried once with the audio re-encoded as AAC at 160 kbit/s.
Timestamps are regenerated and normalised so players can seek.
.P
The source is never modified or deleted unless
.B \-D
is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " DIR"
Write output files into
.I DIR
instead of alongside each input. Inputs from directories are flattened into
.IR DIR .
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-delete
Delete the source
.I .ts
or
.I .mts
after a successful remux.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Overwrite an existing output
.IR .mkv .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS What it does
.IP \(bu 2
Expands directory arguments recursively for files matching
.B *.ts
and
.B *.mts
(case-insensitive).
.IP \(bu 2
Remuxes with
.BR ffmpeg (1)
using
.B \-map 0:v:0 \-map 0:a:0?
and stream copy (the
.B ?
tolerates inputs with no audio stream).
.IP \(bu 2
On mux failure, retries once with the audio re-encoded as AAC 160k.
.IP \(bu 2
Writes to a
.B .part
file and renames on success, so a failed run never leaves a truncated
.B .mkv
behind.
.SS Requirements
.IP \(bu 2
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.SH EXAMPLES
Remux all TS captures under a folder, in place:
.IP
.EX
ts2mkv /mnt/data_storage/ctbrec
.EE
.P
Send the outputs to a separate directory:
.IP
.EX
ts2mkv \-o /mnt/data_storage/Handbraked/rawts /mnt/data_storage/ctbrec
.EE
.P
Remux one file and delete the source when done:
.IP
.EX
ts2mkv \-D recording.ts
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All remuxes succeeded. Skipped files (output already exists) do not count as
failures.
.TP
.B 1
At least one remux failed, or no input files were found.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage (no input given).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
